_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4NzU1MDY3NTk5Njk3NTUxMzY=', 'text': 'After listening to @ShawnRyan762\'s podcast with @samosaur about the Cybertruck explosion in Las Vegas at the Trump Tower and Matt Livelsberger, it just got me thinking!\n\nMatt is a Green Beret with over 20 years of high-special forces operations. If he wanted to, he could have caused major casualties. I say this because I don\'t think he was suicidal or meant to hurt anyone. If he had shot himself in the truck, the person with the suitcase in the road would have noticed it. His body was totally burned, and they identified him only from a tattoo; then, they did a DNA check with his son, which did not match! \n\nSo, Matt did two things:\n\n    1. He faked his death so whoever was chasing him would stop.\n    2.He attracted the attention of everybody, including the media, by sending the Cybertruck to explode in front of Trump Tower.\n\nIf the body is not his, who is it?\n\nAnother topic that attracted my attention in the manifesto he sent to Sam was that he mentioned that the USA and China have a certain technology he calls "gravitic propulsion systems" powered aircraft, which pretty much means flying aircraft or drones that can manipulate gravity. Now, let\'s focus here; why is this so important?\n\nOn Joe Rogan\'s podcast, Bob Lazar, a whistleblower who worked in a classified government project at a secret site near Area 51 reverse-engineering alien spaceships, and he threw out the idea of gravity manipulation. What this means is that a flying drone or spaceship can be here and, in a flash, somewhere else. \n\nThis is a game changer, and the world is not ready for it yet, not ready for a war of drones. That is why the New Jersey drone story was quietly killed when we all knew it was our government.\n\nI am not SUICIDAL if anything happens to me.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '1104564502220161026'